WEBVTT

00:11.910 --> 00:17.830
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

01:30.430 --> 01:31.530
#46: THE WOLFGANG LEAVES THE SEA

01:31.530 --> 01:32.990
#46: THE WOLFGANG LEAVES THE SEA
We'll tackle Rei later...

01:32.990 --> 01:34.990
FOR THE SKYSCRAPERS
We'll tackle Rei later...

01:34.990 --> 01:38.950
There aren't many overlaps, but seems
like we can all team up on the final day.

01:38.950 --> 01:42.710
So whoever's able to log in will try
to work through the scenario

01:42.710 --> 01:45.880
and we'll keep each other updated, right?

01:46.670 --> 01:49.340
Let's call it out for today.

01:49.340 --> 01:54.020
But I don't intend to give up with
the Master of the Abyss treating us like fools.

01:54.640 --> 01:56.760
Day 7 will be our "X Days."

01:56.760 --> 02:03.900
This time we'll be the one to serve the huge
surprise to Ctarnidd and its absurd ability!

02:03.900 --> 02:05.150
Yes!

02:05.530 --> 02:08.320
Serve it good!

02:09.360 --> 02:10.820
On the next day.

02:10.820 --> 02:13.280
5 DAYS UNTIL X DAY
Sunraku aka Rakuro Hizutome

02:13.280 --> 02:15.990
5 DAYS UNTIL X DAY
headed to the big city.

02:15.990 --> 02:16.820
5 DAYS UNTIL X DAY

02:17.490 --> 02:22.330
Our party consists of me,
Akitsuakane, Rust, and Mordo.

02:22.330 --> 02:25.500
You can't send messages in Ruluiath,

02:25.500 --> 02:29.130
so we don't have a means
of contacting Rei.

02:29.130 --> 02:33.290
Well, it's Rei, so I suppose
there's nothing to worry about.

02:34.340 --> 02:35.930
Well, yeah.

02:35.930 --> 02:39.470
Normally you'd use social media
for stuff like this.

02:39.470 --> 02:42.020
As for my charismatic model
and pro gamer friends...

02:42.020 --> 02:46.020
I might mix up my private
and business accounts, so no.

02:46.650 --> 02:52.250
Because of that, we still only
contact each other by e-mail.

02:52.250 --> 02:53.280
Hm?

02:53.690 --> 02:55.400
GGC...

02:55.400 --> 03:01.040
It's a competition held in the middle
of a big international gaming expo.

03:01.040 --> 03:04.870
I never thought I'd be part of it.

03:04.870 --> 03:08.210
Now that I think of it,
this will be my first time

03:08.210 --> 03:12.240
meeting Kei Uomi and Pencilgon—
Towa Amane, in real life.

03:12.670 --> 03:15.970
But Katzo went out of his way

03:15.970 --> 03:18.470
to pay for my trip and stay.

03:18.470 --> 03:21.240
It better not be some crappy hotel.

03:26.310 --> 03:27.060
Huh?

03:28.020 --> 03:28.800
Huh?

03:28.800 --> 03:31.650
We have been waiting for your arrival,
Mister Sunraku.

03:31.650 --> 03:34.490
Mister Kei Uomi
has informed us of your arrival.

03:35.360 --> 03:36.240
Huh?

03:36.240 --> 03:39.200
This way, please.
I'll guide you to your room.

03:39.200 --> 03:40.450
Huh?!

03:42.740 --> 03:44.450
Now, if you excuse me.

03:44.450 --> 03:46.640
Please enjoy your stay, sir.

03:48.040 --> 03:50.880
This... This...

03:51.320 --> 03:54.630
This is a freaking fancy hotel!
What the heck?!

03:54.630 --> 03:56.800
Are you insane, Katzo?!

03:56.800 --> 03:59.890
This ain't the kind of room a high-schooler
can just stay in alone!

03:59.890 --> 04:03.470
This bed's softness is out of this world!

04:03.470 --> 04:06.890
Is this view actually real?
Like, not some CG crap?

04:06.890 --> 04:10.900
This is not some elaborate prank
to snipe me in the head, right?

04:11.860 --> 04:13.690
T-This is...!

04:13.690 --> 04:17.070
Notorious for its hefty price
no commoner can buy...

04:17.070 --> 04:20.490
...the latest-of-the-art
Full-Dive system!

04:21.570 --> 04:24.620
No wonder a pro gamer
picked this place!

04:24.620 --> 04:27.580
The room here comes
with a fancy custom rig?

04:27.580 --> 04:29.500
This is so amazing,
I can't relax!

04:29.500 --> 04:31.880
How am I supposed to?!

04:31.880 --> 04:34.130
Just how serious is he about this?!

04:34.130 --> 04:37.590
Or he's just so insanely rich
that he got bugged perception of money?!

04:37.590 --> 04:39.590
Get your ass down here already, Katzo!

04:39.590 --> 04:43.680
Hey, dude! What's up with this hotel?!
It's not some massive prank, is it?

04:43.680 --> 04:45.390
Oh, you made it?

04:45.390 --> 04:49.690
Pencilgon said she's here too.
I'll call our other teammate.

04:49.690 --> 04:50.850
Just wait in your room.

04:50.850 --> 04:54.440
Huh? Our "other teammate"?

04:54.440 --> 04:57.990
Oh, right.
It is a four-on-four team battle.

05:00.150 --> 05:02.530
Heya, Sunraku!

05:03.030 --> 05:07.410
It's the super charismatic model
Towa Amane, in the flesh.

05:08.120 --> 05:09.830
Oh, Pencilgon?

05:09.830 --> 05:11.540
Yeah, open up.

05:11.540 --> 05:12.670
Y-Yeah, coming.

05:13.500 --> 05:15.420
Hm, wait...

05:15.880 --> 05:19.800
This will be my first time meeting up
face-to-face with them in real life.

05:20.250 --> 05:23.260
I'll be meeting up with a charismatic
model and a pro gamer.

05:23.260 --> 05:28.180
It never bothered me in video games,
but I'm the only one who hasn't shown my face.

05:28.600 --> 05:31.810
- Hello? Sunraku?
- Isn't this actually my big chance?

05:32.200 --> 05:35.940
Is it really okay for their first impression
of me to just be that of an average teen?

05:35.940 --> 05:38.280
No, of course not!

05:38.280 --> 05:39.990
It'd be such a waste!

05:40.530 --> 05:44.660
I'll give them the biggest impact
I can manage right now!

05:44.660 --> 05:47.410
Come on, what are you doing there?

05:47.410 --> 05:50.250
Just open up already.

05:50.250 --> 05:53.290
If you don't, I'll call the police
saying there's a stranger inside.

05:56.450 --> 06:01.550
Hey, hey! We finally got
the chance to talk face-to-fa—

06:10.910 --> 06:13.310
Sorry for all the rush.

06:13.310 --> 06:17.900
But the sooner we all meet up,
the better it is, right, Meg?

06:17.900 --> 06:20.110
That's fine by me.

06:20.110 --> 06:23.310
But are these other two good?

06:23.310 --> 06:25.950
Are they good enough
to fill in for pro gamers?

06:25.950 --> 06:29.300
Yeah. You have my words.

06:29.950 --> 06:31.950
That means a lot coming from you.

06:32.540 --> 06:37.460
Besides, there's a solid reason
why I chose them.

06:37.880 --> 06:39.050
Reason?

06:39.050 --> 06:41.290
You should see them
with your own eyes.

06:41.290 --> 06:45.050
Well, this will be my first time meeting
them in real life as well, though.

06:45.760 --> 06:49.850
They might do nothing
but silly stuff in games,

06:49.850 --> 06:52.010
but you can trust their skill.

06:56.730 --> 07:00.730
I didn't think you'd be that
serious about hiding your face!

07:01.900 --> 07:03.990
It turned out there really
was a stranger here!

07:03.990 --> 07:06.740
Ow, ow! The laughing
is giving me the cramps!

07:06.740 --> 07:08.450
I'm not trying to hide it or anything!

07:08.450 --> 07:11.950
I'm just wearing this gas mask
I got as a preorder bonus as a joke!

07:12.410 --> 07:14.790
It's a rare piece, y'know!
Out of print!

07:15.290 --> 07:20.250
Stop it! That's barely an explanation either!
It's hilarious!

07:22.090 --> 07:26.260
Sorry, Meg. These guys also
do silly stuff in real life.

07:27.970 --> 07:29.970
Hey there, pro gamer.

07:29.970 --> 07:31.890
Is she that other member
you talked about?

07:31.890 --> 07:33.220
Yeah.

07:33.220 --> 07:39.650
Just me like, she's a member of Nitro Squad
who's free for the next two days.

07:39.650 --> 07:40.980
Megumi Natsume.

07:40.980 --> 07:44.190
PRO GAMER - MEGUMI NATSUME
NITRO SQUAD MEMBER

07:44.190 --> 07:45.860
H-Hello.

07:45.860 --> 07:49.450
Oh, I've seen you in a magazine before.

07:49.450 --> 07:50.490
Nice to meet 'cha!

07:50.490 --> 07:52.120
I don't know her.

07:52.550 --> 07:53.580
Kei...

07:53.580 --> 07:57.830
Meg, I know you have a lot to say,
but let's get inside first.

07:58.310 --> 08:00.130
I want us to discuss the competition.

08:00.130 --> 08:02.090
Oh, right off the bat?

08:02.090 --> 08:03.840
You sure are pumped up, Katzo.

08:05.340 --> 08:09.430
Our opponent is the strongest
top-ranked team in the US.

08:09.860 --> 08:13.910
Meanwhile, we're a team cobbled
together at the last minute.

08:14.430 --> 08:21.440
But what if I say there's a way for us,
and especially us, to defeat them?

08:21.440 --> 08:23.230
Don't you want to hear it?

08:23.230 --> 08:24.360
Sunraku. Pencilgon.

08:24.360 --> 08:25.650
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON
Sunraku. Pencilgon.

08:25.650 --> 08:26.940
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

08:27.950 --> 08:30.450
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

08:32.580 --> 08:36.120
How long does this pencil
intend to keep on laughing?

08:36.120 --> 08:39.790
And how long do you intend
to wear that gas mask?

08:39.790 --> 08:42.590
I lost my timing to take it off.
Let it be.

08:42.590 --> 08:45.630
That damn noise of your mask
is annoying me.

08:45.630 --> 08:48.550
It's like your entire existence is a joke.

08:49.800 --> 08:53.050
But I'm surprised the super famous
charismatic model

08:53.050 --> 08:55.890
managed to find the time for this.

08:55.890 --> 09:00.480
Oh, you know. I look good in pictures
whenever and wherever I am.

09:00.480 --> 09:03.810
My work sessions don't actually
take that much time.

09:03.810 --> 09:06.230
Oh?

09:06.230 --> 09:10.110
I didn't pick up at first because
of the whole gas mask thing,

09:10.110 --> 09:12.880
but she is that famous model,
Towa Amane.

09:13.450 --> 09:16.330
A guy in a gas mask
and a charismatic model...

09:16.760 --> 09:17.690
Kei.

09:18.830 --> 09:23.080
Are you really telling me these two are
your secret weapon against Star Rain?

09:23.460 --> 09:27.710
Is "Star Rain" the name of
that strongest in the US team?

09:27.710 --> 09:28.630
Yes.

09:28.880 --> 09:32.890
Star Rain is a top-class
fighting game team.

09:32.890 --> 09:36.010
Wow, look at all those muscles.
Must be suffocating to be around them.

09:36.010 --> 09:40.020
Are you sure they play fighting games,
and not actually fighting in the street?

09:40.020 --> 09:44.190
They say Johnson on the far right
can crush an apple with one hand.

09:44.190 --> 09:47.480
Wow! That's like the most
American team ever.

09:47.480 --> 09:49.070
What do you mean by that?

09:49.420 --> 09:52.610
Oh, but there's one
cute girl among them, too.

09:52.610 --> 09:55.290
The group's female
representation, I suppose?

09:55.290 --> 09:58.150
She's Silvia Goldberg.

09:58.620 --> 10:02.920
If you ask who's
the best player in the US,

10:02.920 --> 10:05.630
her name will definitely come up first.

10:06.070 --> 10:07.630
Oh...

10:07.990 --> 10:11.880
Her name first popped out five years ago.

10:11.880 --> 10:15.200
She was playing in the amateur division
of a certain fighting game tournament.

10:15.200 --> 10:18.850
She took zero damage
from her first match to the final,

10:18.850 --> 10:20.520
sealing her victory with flying colors.

10:20.520 --> 10:21.390
Wow.

10:21.390 --> 10:23.690
In the subsequent exhibition matches,

10:23.690 --> 10:27.020
she took round after round
against pro gamers,

10:27.020 --> 10:29.230
showing off her overwhelming talent.

10:29.730 --> 10:34.590
And with that ridiculous performance,
her name was spread wide,

10:34.590 --> 10:37.530
shocking the international
fighting game scene.

10:38.200 --> 10:40.870
After her shocking debut,

10:40.870 --> 10:43.710
she was scouted by a pro gaming team.

10:44.200 --> 10:50.380
Within a year, a fighter-specific team was
formed with Silvia at the core— Star Rain.

10:51.130 --> 10:58.890
Five years on, Silvia continues to set
shining records as a top star pro gamer.

10:58.890 --> 11:02.310
The best pro gamer,
in name and deed, eh?

11:02.310 --> 11:04.810
That's some "final boss" material.

11:04.810 --> 11:07.230
And also, she got good looks.

11:07.230 --> 11:11.320
She's like a super strong supporting character
who'd get first place in popularity pools.

11:11.320 --> 11:15.360
Oh, yeah,
the type that overshines the protagonist.

11:15.360 --> 11:19.740
It goes without saying, but the other three
members are also top-class pro gamers.

11:19.740 --> 11:23.000
And you told me that we'd
have a chance of winning

11:23.000 --> 11:26.790
as long as we have these two,
who aren't even pro gamers?

11:28.790 --> 11:32.670
Yeah, we'd like to hear
about that too.

11:34.220 --> 11:38.760
True. Normally, there's no way
we'd have a chance.

11:39.300 --> 11:43.350
I hate to admit it,
but Silvia is scarily good.

11:43.350 --> 11:45.350
I've fought her a few times before,

11:45.350 --> 11:49.310
but never once I was close to winning,
and the closest I got was a draw once.

11:49.770 --> 11:52.820
But for this match,
there's a breakthrough.

11:53.250 --> 11:54.650
A breakthrough?

11:55.110 --> 11:56.010
And that is?

11:58.140 --> 12:01.950
These two play Shangri-La Frontier.

12:03.810 --> 12:05.410
SLF?

12:05.410 --> 12:07.050
I'll explain from the beginning.

12:07.920 --> 12:11.040
First off, the game we will be playing...

12:11.920 --> 12:14.670
...is Galaxia Heroes: Chaos.

12:14.670 --> 12:18.050
It's a VR fighting game set
to be released this Autumn.

12:18.050 --> 12:20.260
So it's not out yet?

12:20.260 --> 12:22.260
Wait, "Galaxia"?

12:22.260 --> 12:25.980
Wasn't that also the name of the publisher
of the comic book you told me to read?

12:25.980 --> 12:27.480
That's right.

12:27.480 --> 12:30.480
The characters in this game
are all heroes and villains

12:30.480 --> 12:33.510
from comic books published
by Galaxia Comics.

12:34.320 --> 12:40.570
A crossover fighting game that features
a bunch of characters from the same publisher.

12:40.570 --> 12:43.450
That's what Galaxia Heroes is.

12:43.450 --> 12:48.330
Oh, right. Come to think of it, I haven't
actually read that American comic.

12:48.330 --> 12:49.620
I only browsed them a bit.

12:49.620 --> 12:51.500
I asked you guys to read it!

12:51.500 --> 12:53.840
Knowing the characters
and settings is important!

12:53.840 --> 12:55.880
Good grief!

12:55.880 --> 12:59.720
Anyway, this is a video game series
and you can play the previous one.

12:59.720 --> 13:03.600
But the one we will be playing in
the competition will be their latest installment.

13:03.600 --> 13:09.100
And our stage in GGC also serves
as a preview of that for the public.

13:09.100 --> 13:14.820
An exhibition team match between
our team Nitro Squad and Star Rain.

13:14.820 --> 13:19.240
And what's about us playing SLF
has to do with that?

13:19.240 --> 13:22.950
The latest installment
Galaxy Heroes: Chaos

13:22.950 --> 13:27.870
is co-developed as a tie-in with
the company behind SLF, the U.E.S.

13:28.370 --> 13:30.250
The company behind SLF?

13:30.250 --> 13:36.000
The U.E.S. offered their tech that is several
generations ahead of their competition.

13:36.000 --> 13:42.510
In other words, the game's gonna provide
virtual reality on a level beyond any other.

13:42.510 --> 13:47.250
It will probably be the second game
in what you'd call a "SLF gen" game.

13:47.810 --> 13:52.480
That's why this installment is not
going to be like any other before.

13:52.480 --> 13:55.230
Oh, I see.

13:55.230 --> 13:57.780
I get what you're saying now.

13:58.480 --> 14:02.860
There's no info on the Star Rain members
having already played SLF.

14:02.860 --> 14:04.700
Our match will be
the day after tomorrow.

14:04.700 --> 14:08.410
They'll only have two days
to get to know the game system.

14:08.410 --> 14:15.130
But we have the advantage of playing SLF
and are already used to the system.

14:15.130 --> 14:16.210
That's right.

14:16.210 --> 14:20.380
We have the advantage of familiarity.
That's our breakthrough.

14:22.510 --> 14:26.470
W-Wait, I understand
the logic and everything.

14:26.470 --> 14:29.160
But our opponent is not
the kind of team

14:29.160 --> 14:31.890
that anyone can beat just because
they're familiar with SLF.

14:31.890 --> 14:33.310
Meg.

14:33.310 --> 14:36.520
That's why it must be these two.

14:36.950 --> 14:41.030
Remember what I told you?
You can trust their skill.

14:45.030 --> 14:49.200
Oh, can you repeat that?
Did you actually compliment us just now, Katzo?

14:49.200 --> 14:51.330
H-Hey, stay back.

14:51.330 --> 14:53.750
Aww, so that's what you were
thinking this whole time?

14:53.750 --> 14:56.040
That's so cute of you.

14:56.040 --> 14:58.130
Get your hand off me!

14:58.130 --> 15:00.170
Damn it, that was a slip of the tongue.

15:01.710 --> 15:04.800
Well, whatever.
It's true, anyway.

15:05.300 --> 15:06.470
Sunraku.

15:06.470 --> 15:07.550
Hmm?

15:07.550 --> 15:12.560
Pencil... or Towa Amane, should I say?

15:12.560 --> 15:15.310
This is our first time
meeting each other in real life.

15:15.310 --> 15:19.000
To be honest, I was worried
if you two would actually come or not.

15:21.570 --> 15:24.570
But thanks for coming, both of you.

15:26.950 --> 15:29.910
Well, I guess it's official now.

15:29.910 --> 15:30.740
Yeah.

15:35.580 --> 15:38.500
They might do nothing
but silly stuff in games,

15:38.500 --> 15:40.590
but you can trust their skill.

15:40.590 --> 15:45.380
Kei takes a lot of pride in his gaming.
So for him to say that...

15:47.010 --> 15:48.050
Fine.

15:49.340 --> 15:53.350
If you insist that much,
I'll trust these two.

15:53.350 --> 15:56.820
In fact, I'm interested in both of you,
seeing how much Kei sees in you.

15:57.480 --> 16:03.600
So will you mind if I play against you
and see how strong you really are?

16:06.820 --> 16:08.490
As you wish.

16:09.490 --> 16:14.370
Man, that guy never took
that gas mask off till the end.

16:14.370 --> 16:17.290
I bet he's planning to keep
that on the whole event.

16:17.290 --> 16:19.210
Why's he so stubborn about it?

16:19.210 --> 16:22.500
More importantly, you better
read the Galaxia comics!

16:22.500 --> 16:24.380
You'll understand
the character much mo—

16:24.380 --> 16:27.260
Oops! My room's on this floor!

16:29.760 --> 16:31.470
See you later, Meg!

16:31.470 --> 16:34.410
I'm open to taking you on
whenever you're ready!

16:40.690 --> 16:42.240
You better watch out.

16:42.240 --> 16:46.320
There's no way she'll
fight you like normal.

16:46.320 --> 16:49.780
Kei, I know you rate those
two pretty highly and all,

16:50.200 --> 16:52.370
but are you thinking
they'll actually beat me?

16:53.910 --> 16:54.990
Who knows?

16:54.990 --> 16:57.410
I'm well aware of their skill.

16:57.410 --> 17:00.290
But although they've played SLF,

17:00.290 --> 17:03.250
this will be their first time playing
a Galaxia series game.

17:03.250 --> 17:06.340
As neither of them knows
the characters' traits yet,

17:06.340 --> 17:08.630
there's no telling how it will turn out.

17:08.630 --> 17:10.300
But if I have to say,

17:10.300 --> 17:13.280
I'd be happier if you
could beat them for me.

17:14.230 --> 17:18.550
I bet it'd be fun to see them
all anguished over it, too.

17:22.520 --> 17:25.000
Anyway, let me know your thoughts later.

17:28.610 --> 17:31.570
"There's no telling how it will turn out"?

17:32.240 --> 17:34.030
Does he mean...

17:34.030 --> 17:38.690
...if we're fighting on equal ground,
they'd be better than me?

17:39.830 --> 17:40.910
Wow...

17:40.910 --> 17:44.210
Wow, this VR chair is amazing!

17:44.210 --> 17:47.840
It's got less latency than a helmet type,
and much smoother, too!

17:47.840 --> 17:50.840
It's like I can operate my avatar
almost purely on instinct!

17:50.840 --> 17:55.930
Thanks a lot, Katzo!
This alone made the trip worth it!

17:55.930 --> 17:57.310
Also...

17:57.310 --> 18:00.180
I tested out all the characters
to get a feel for them,

18:00.180 --> 18:04.810
but it really does seem like
it uses the SLF tech.

18:04.810 --> 18:07.940
REAL
One of the disadvantages of Full-Dive games

18:07.940 --> 18:10.990
AVATAR
is that it'd feel unnatural when your avatar

18:10.990 --> 18:13.320
AVATAR
is too different from your real-life body.

18:13.320 --> 18:18.330
In fighting games, the first step is getting
used to your preferred character's body!

18:18.750 --> 18:24.640
I don't know how they did it,
but they completely solved that issue in SLF.

18:24.640 --> 18:27.750
No matter what body type
your avatar is,

18:27.750 --> 18:32.590
you can easily control it as if
it's your own body you grew up with.

18:32.590 --> 18:37.470
And Galaxia Heroes: Chaos
inherited that trait properly.

18:37.470 --> 18:40.680
For now, I'll list up characters
that felt good to me.

18:40.680 --> 18:41.980
First, we have...

18:42.810 --> 18:44.020
Ranzo.

18:44.020 --> 18:47.980
An old man-type hero character who wields
two Japanese swords at the same time.

18:47.980 --> 18:50.820
His combat style is close
to Sunraku's from SLF,

18:50.820 --> 18:55.030
and his special "iai" moves offer
near-instant movement, a big plus.

18:55.530 --> 18:57.070
Cursed Prison.

18:57.070 --> 19:01.160
A villain who has his powers
restrained by his cursed suit of armor.

19:01.160 --> 19:06.000
He can absorb things like cars
and rubble to power up his armor.

19:06.000 --> 19:09.420
But care is needed to make up
for his low mobility.

19:09.420 --> 19:13.170
It is a fun character to use with
his high-risk, high-return moves.

19:13.920 --> 19:15.230
Metius.

19:15.230 --> 19:18.720
A character with outstanding mobility,
allowing him to seize territorial advantage

19:18.720 --> 19:22.180
over his opponents with his bullrush
advances that can easily cover any distance.

19:22.180 --> 19:27.020
His weakness is that he needs to come
to a full stop to do sharp curves,

19:27.020 --> 19:30.520
and due to his low defense, so he has to
remain constantly on the move to survive.

19:30.520 --> 19:34.150
Cursed Prison is his nemesis
in the original comics.

19:34.730 --> 19:36.110
Twinkle Pixie.

19:36.110 --> 19:38.950
Her cute fairy-like look is just a front.

19:38.950 --> 19:42.600
In fact, she's an incredibly
annoying opponent to fight.

19:42.600 --> 19:45.930
Most of her combos involve going in close,
restricting her opponent's moves,

19:45.930 --> 19:48.000
then bludgeoning them,

19:48.000 --> 19:51.750
making her more of a malicious devil
than a benevolent fairy.

19:52.880 --> 19:54.340
Psy-borg Lord.

19:54.340 --> 19:58.680
A character with the combined power of Esper
and cyborg who fight using projectiles.

19:58.680 --> 20:00.970
Landing his wealth
of step-driven skills

20:00.970 --> 20:04.380
lets you one-sidedly fire off
a constant barrage of strikes.

20:04.380 --> 20:06.600
He's all but doomed if his
opponent gets too close,

20:06.600 --> 20:09.130
so playing as him requires
a lot of pinpoint movement.

20:09.690 --> 20:12.270
Well, that's about all of them.

20:12.270 --> 20:14.210
I'll start by picking among these five.

20:15.400 --> 20:16.570
Hmm?

20:17.280 --> 20:20.780
It's almost time for our match.
Can you log in?

20:20.780 --> 20:24.200
Oh, Natsume's already
itching to test me out!

20:24.200 --> 20:25.580
Well, perfect.

20:25.580 --> 20:28.210
I don't care if she is a pro gamer!

20:28.210 --> 20:30.250
I'm gonna make her admit that I'm good!

20:39.360 --> 20:40.180
Hero vs Villain battle established.

20:40.180 --> 20:42.140
HERO VS VILLAIN BATTLE ESTABLISHED
Hero vs Villain battle established.

20:42.140 --> 20:42.930
DEMOLITION TIME PROVIDED

20:42.930 --> 20:43.970
DEMOLITION TIME PROVIDED
So Natsume chose a villain, huh?

20:43.970 --> 20:45.100
FOR VILLAIN PLAYER NU2MEG
So Natsume chose a villain, huh?

20:51.650 --> 20:54.900
Moving the Hero Player
Sunraku to the area.

20:55.690 --> 20:57.740
This game is based on

20:57.740 --> 20:58.820
CHAOS CITY
an American superhero comic.

20:58.820 --> 21:00.780
CHAOS CITY
And it has one key difference

21:00.780 --> 21:02.170
CHAOS CITY
from other fighters.

21:02.170 --> 21:02.910
CHAOS CITY

21:02.910 --> 21:05.370
CHAOS CITY
Here when the heroes act heroically,

21:05.370 --> 21:08.080
or when the villains act evilly,

21:08.080 --> 21:10.790
the game will be in your favor.

21:10.790 --> 21:11.670
RANZO - PLAYER: SUNRAKU
the game will be in your favor.

21:11.670 --> 21:13.960
RANZO - PLAYER: SUNRAKU

21:13.960 --> 21:15.340
RANZO - PLAYER: SUNRAKU
Wow~

21:15.340 --> 21:18.590
Natsume is already
causing quite the scene.

21:18.590 --> 21:21.090
Mommy, my leg hurts!

21:21.090 --> 21:24.100
Climb on my back, quick!
We have to get out of here!

21:38.280 --> 21:39.860
Are you all right?

21:40.280 --> 21:43.370
Ah, thank you very much!

21:43.370 --> 21:44.160
HEROIC GAUGE

21:44.160 --> 21:47.580
HEROIC GAUGE
All right. Megu Natsume, pro gamer.

21:47.580 --> 21:49.700
HEROIC GAUGE
I can't wait to see what kind of play style

21:49.700 --> 21:50.870
HEROIC GAUGE
are you going to show me.

21:54.460 --> 21:57.170
Argh, stop it!

21:57.170 --> 21:58.880
Let me go!

21:58.880 --> 22:01.380
VILLANIC GAUGE

22:01.380 --> 22:04.010
Just you watch, Kei.

22:04.010 --> 22:06.970
YGGDRYA - PLAYER: NU2MEG
I'll make it clear who's the stronger one,

22:06.970 --> 22:08.890
YGGDRYA - PLAYER: NU2MEG
